1. Preserved stage-11a results and corrected claim
-------------------------------------------------
Preserved: h0 contains the full delta*z*d/dz term; Psi0=z^N/sqrt(N!);
the complete nondegeneracy condition; energy through lambda^4; wavefunction
recursion through lambda^4; the exact tridiagonal Bargmann recurrence; the
upper 0F1 edge sum; the terminating lower 1F1 edge; and the absence of a
direct Weber reduction.  The sentence saying that the edge sum did not
reproduce the large-z WKB balance was too strong.  It reproduces the formal
leading WKB exponent and leading algebraic prefactor, but supplies no global
WKB theorem or uniform error estimate.

The upper edge is the order-k coefficient of |N+k>, generated by k monotone
upward steps.  The first upper subdiagonal is the order-k coefficient of
|N+k-2>; it has one downward step relative to that endpoint and, from the
appropriate orders onward, the fold proportional to e_N^(2).

2. Upper-edge differential equation
------------------------------------
For b=2N+2delta and Y0=0F1(;b;-2lambda*z), direct differentiation of its
series gives
    z Y0'' + b Y0' + 2 lambda Y0 = 0.
The equation was checked numerically at 70 decimal digits for complex b and
three complex z values; maximum scaled residual was below 1e-65.

3. Exact Bargmann residual
--------------------------
For Psi_edge=z^N Y0/sqrt(N!), substitution in the exact equation and use of
the edge ODE gives exactly
 R_edge=z^N/sqrt(N!)*[lambda Y0' + lambda*N*Y0/z
                       -(epsilon-e_N)Y0].
The derivative terms are the omitted downward action; the last term begins
with -lambda^2 e_N^(2)Y0.  They encode returning paths and subsequent
diagonals.  With x=-2lambda*z fixed the residual is z^N O(lambda^2), while
the retained edge equation is z^N O(1).  This is formal and not a relative
bound near zeros.

4. 0F1--Bessel relation, branches, and sectors
----------------------------------------------
For b not in {0,-1,-2,...}, on a consistently chosen Log/square-root branch,
  0F1(;b;x)=Gamma(b)x^((1-b)/2) I_(b-1)(2sqrt(x))
            =Gamma(b)(-x)^((1-b)/2) J_(b-1)(2sqrt(-x)).
The products analytically continue to the single-valued entire 0F1.  On the
principal x branch and away from Stokes boundaries the dominant I saddle is
Gamma(b)/(2sqrt(pi))*x^((1-2b)/4)*exp(2sqrt(x)); continuation adds the
exp(-2sqrt(x)) saddle with the I-function Stokes phase.  The J form displays
the oscillatory phases exp[+/-i(2sqrt(-x)-pi(b-1)/2-pi/4)].  The identity was
checked for three complex (b,x) cases at 70 digits; maximum relative error
was 9.21e-72.

5. Independent WKB calculation
------------------------------
The gauge Psi=z^(-delta) exp(lambda/z) u gives the exact normal form
 u''+K u=0,
 K=2lambda/z+(-2epsilon+delta-delta^2)/z^2
   +2(1-delta)lambda/z^3-lambda^2/z^4.
For |lambda*z|>>1 the leading eikonal equation is
 (1/2)z^2(S')^2+lambda*z=0, so
 S'=+/-sqrt(-2lambda/z), S=+/-2sqrt(-2lambda*z), on one fixed branch.
The first transport factor is z^(-delta)(-2lambda/z)^(-1/4), with z-power
z^(1/4-delta).

6. Match verdict
----------------
The Bessel exponent is exactly the formal leading WKB exponent.  Its power is
also identical: z^N*x^((1-2b)/4) is proportional to z^(1/4-delta).
The gauge exp(lambda/z), energy-dependent transport, return paths, and higher
diagonals are missing.  Fixed x=O(1) alone is not a WKB large-argument limit;
the comparison additionally needs 1<<|x| in sectors with separated saddles.

7. First subdiagonal recurrence
-------------------------------
Write Psi/(z^N/sqrt(N!))=Y0(x)+lambda^2 Y1(x)+O(lambda^4),
Y1=sum_{m=-1}^infinity d_m x^m, a_m=1/[m!(b)_m].  Then
 d_-1=-4N/(b-2), d_0=0,
 d_m=[d_(m-1)+4(m+N+1)a_(m+1)+2e_N^(2)a_m]/[m(m+b-1)], m>=1.
The m=0 solvability condition is exactly the known e_N^(2).  This separates
the single-return source 2Y0'+2N Y0/x from the energy source e_N^(2)Y0.

8. Generating function
----------------------
The exact summed generating function is the intermediate-normalized Laurent
solution of
 L_b Y1=2Y0'+2N Y0/x+e_N^(2)Y0,
 L_b=(x^2/2)d^2/dx^2+(b*x/2)d/dx-x/2.
Variation of parameters uses 0F1(;b;x) and x^(1-b)0F1(;2-b;x).  The Laurent
normalization d_0=0 removes the homogeneous ambiguity.  Its coefficients
agree symbolically with the full RS recurrence through order lambda^6.

9. BB hierarchy assessment
---------------------------
Exactly two upper diagonals have now been summed.  The new term has p=2 and
is a relative lambda^2*Y1/Y0 correction.  Locally it can be represented as a
prefactor or first logarithmic correction, but it is not merely a shift of
the Bessel parameter and does not establish a completed iterative BB
hierarchy.

10. Typographical corrections
------------------------------
The Bargmann recurrence now uses thin-space multiplication instead of commas:
f sqrt(n) c_(n-1)+f*sqrt(n+1)c_(n+1).  The literal PDF text "qquad" came from
an actually missing backslash before qquad in manuscript.tex; the source now
contains \\qquad and the zero-order fraction was modernized.  pdftotext now
extracts "N in N0" without "qquad"; visual inspection confirms the spacing.

